          "literatureReview": "Blood group testing is fundamental in transfusion medicine and clinical practice. The ABO system classifies blood into four main types (A, B, AB, O) based on antigens present on red blood cells, while the Rh system determines the presence of the D antigen. Accurate blood typing prevents hemolytic transfusion reactions and is essential for safe blood transfusions, prenatal care, and organ transplantation. The test uses serological methods to detect specific antibodies and antigens."
